  "description": "The DUPKEY half of the shared arm. app/cbl/COUSR01C.cbl:260 and :261 are two consecutive WHEN clauses with no statements between them - COBOL's way of writing 'either of these' - so DFHRESP(DUPKEY) and DFHRESP(DUPREC) run the same four statements at :262-266. This case FORCES RESP 15, and the forcing is deliberate rather than convenient: a WRITE against a base KSDS reports DUPREC for a colliding primary key and never DUPKEY, which CICS raises on an alternate index, so no arrangement of the seeded rows can reach this half. The message is 'User ID already exist...' and the cursor goes to USERIDL - note USERIDL and not the FNAMEL the WHEN OTHER arm at :272 uses. INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS does not run here, so the five typed values stay on the screen for the operator to correct.",
